{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1tdFUQfvJwh8DMkDhy2", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I signed off on the sweep. One possible bug is still open: I filed it twice and the developer said both times they could not reproduce it. My confidence is low, 0.4.\n\n- **Open issue (sort sheet):** Grouping by due date showed \"Descending\" when I first opened the sheet. After I set it to Ascending, switching Grouping to None and then to By priority brought it back as Descending. The unresolved question is whether Descending is the intended default.\n- **Search:** Results were correct for each query I tried and refreshed as I deleted characters. I tried \"pa\", \"pay\", \"litres\" (a notes match), \"GUIDE\" (a link in the notes), and \"zzz\" (no match, which gave the empty message).\n- **Repeating tasks:**\n  - Custom weekly repeat on Mon and Wed saved and showed \"Repeats weekly on Mon, Wed\".\n  - Completing Pay rent (monthly) moved it from Dec 4 to January 4, 2027, and Undo put it back.\n- **Weekday order:** The custom repeat picker lists Sunday first (S M T W T F S). I assumed that matches this device's locale and did not test other locales.\n- **Not tested:** rotating the screen.\n\nI changed Buy milk's repeat to weekly on Mon and Wed and left it that way. The sort grouping is now By priority, which I also left changed."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 414, "cache_read_input_tokens": 59309, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 414}, "output_tokens": 447, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "30ab5589-4f02-4917-ac3b-18a87d6ba8cf", "uuid": "66e7aa75-e22f-4b00-9ac6-1b984f